($q$Acid-adjusted orange juice$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://blog.modernistpantry.com/advice/how-to-acid-adjust-juices/$q$, $q$producer$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Orange to lime acidity: 3.2 g citric and 2 g malic per 100 ml juice; scaled to 1 litre.$q$),
($q$Acid-adjusted orange juice$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.diffordsguide.com/forum/LJbdDL$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Same chart per litre of juice: orange to lime, 32 g citric and 20 g malic.$q$),
($q$Acid-adjusted orange juice$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://www.tastingtable.com/1884078/how-long-fresh-orange-juice-last-fridge$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for plain fresh orange juice, less acidic than ours: 2 to 3 days in the fridge; we take the shorter end.$q$),
($q$Agave syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/articles/not-too-sweet-ok-how-to-use-simple-demerara-cane-honey-agave-cocktail-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$2 parts agave nectar to 1 part water by weight gives close to 50 Brix, so it balances like simple. Scaled to 1 kg nectar. We use this ratio.$q$),
($q$Agave syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://imbibemagazine.com/recipe/agave-syrup-recipe$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Second source runs 1 cup agave to 1 cup water (1:1 by volume), a thinner syrup; we use 2:1 by weight from Punch.$q$),
($q$Agave syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://imbibemagazine.com/recipe/agave-syrup-recipe$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Refrigerated, up to 2 weeks.$q$),
($q$Bacon fat-infused bourbon$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/recipes/bentons-bacon-infused-bourbon/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Punch (PDT): 1.5 oz (45 ml) bacon fat to 750 ml bourbon, infuse 4 hours, freeze 2 hours, strain. Scaled to 700 ml about 42; our 40 g is within 10%.$q$),
($q$Bacon fat-infused bourbon$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://drinksworld.com/fat-washing-guide/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$General fat-washing guide: fat-washed spirits, kept in the fridge, last about 1 to 2 weeks. We take the shorter end.$q$),
($q$Banana syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://cocktail-society.com/wprm_print/5817$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$1 ripe banana (about 3 oz), 3 oz cane sugar, 1.5 oz water, pinch of salt: 2 : 2 : 1. Macerate 3 hours, warm 5 minutes, rest overnight, strain. Scaled to 300 g banana: 300 g sugar, 150 ml water.$q$),
($q$Banana syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://cocktail-society.com/wprm_print/5817$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for this same recipe: fridge, at least three weeks.$q$),
