($q$Raspberry shrub$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.ccfruitandnuts.ucanr.edu/sites/default/files/2023-10/389540.pdf$q$, $q$law$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$UC Master Food Preservers give equal parts fruit, sugar and vinegar (1:1:1) as the common shrub formula, macerating fruit with sugar about 24 hours before adding vinegar. 500 g of each.$q$),
($q$Raspberry shrub$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://www.ccfruitandnuts.ucanr.edu/sites/default/files/2023-10/389540.pdf$q$, $q$law$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$General shrub storage advice for the same cold-process 1:1:1 shrubs: refrigerated, up to a year. We keep our shorter 8 weeks.$q$),
($q$Raspberry syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/recipes/clover-club/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Julie Reiner: 1/2 cup raspberries, 1 cup sugar, 1/2 cup water, macerated 30 min. Converted (raspberries about 123 g a cup per USDA tables, sugar 200 g, water 120 ml) and scaled x2.5. Reiner adds 15 ml vodka to fortify; we leave it out, as Imbibe does.$q$),
($q$Raspberry syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://imbibemagazine.com/raspberry-syrup-recipe$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Second source: 2 cups demerara sugar, 1 cup water, 1 cup raspberries, the same 1 : 2 : 1 proportions by volume as Reiner. Agrees.$q$),
($q$Raspberry syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://imbibemagazine.com/raspberry-syrup-recipe$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for Imbibe's raspberry syrup, same sugar level as ours and no spirit: up to 2 weeks in the fridge.$q$),
($q$Rhubarb syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.lurch.de/en/recipes/Recipes/Rhubarb-syrup-for-lemonade$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Lurch: 400 g rhubarb, 400 g sugar, 600 ml water, 1 tsp vanilla extract; boil, simmer 5 minutes, infuse about 24 hours, strain, reboil, bottle. Source batch as written.$q$),
($q$Rhubarb syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://bakesbybrownsugar.com/wprm_print/rhubarb-syrup$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for a less sweet rhubarb syrup (454 g rhubarb, 480 ml water, 200 g sugar): fridge, up to two weeks.$q$),
($q$Rich demerara syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/articles/essential-guide-cocktail-recipe-sweeteners-agave-demerara-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Demerara syrup is most often two parts sugar to one part water. Scaled to 1 kg sugar.$q$),
($q$Rich demerara syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.amazingfoodmadeeasy.com/info/modernist-recipes/more/demerara-syrup-recipe$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Its demerara syrup is 200 g demerara to 100 g water (2:1 by weight), plus optional extras we leave out.$q$),
($q$Rich honey syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.diffordsguide.com/cocktails/recipe/965/honey-daiquiri$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Honey syrup at 3 parts honey to 1 part water by weight. Scaled to 1.5 kg honey.$q$),
($q$Rich simple syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.diffordsguide.com/encyclopedia/3593/cocktails/2-to-1-rich-sugar-syrup-versus-1-to-1-simple-syrup$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Two parts sugar to one part water, by weight in its example (2 kg sugar to 1 kg water). Scaled to 1 kg sugar.$q$),
($q$Rich simple syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/articles/not-too-sweet-ok-how-to-use-simple-demerara-cane-honey-agave-cocktail-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Rich simple is two parts white sugar to one part water, about 66.6 Brix. Agrees with Difford's.$q$),
($q$Rich simple syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://alcademics.com/simple-syrup-its-good-to-be-rich/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Side by side fridge test: 2:1 syrup lasted six months before clouding. We keep 8 weeks, well inside that.$q$),
($q$Saline solution$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.americastestkitchen.com/articles/6186-this-ingredient-makes-every-cocktail-pop$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$20% saline: 80 g water to 20 g kosher salt (non-iodised), stirred to dissolve; tested by the drop in cocktails. Scaled to 1 kg.$q$),
($q$Saline solution$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://cocktailsandbars.com/salt-in-cocktails/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$20 g sea salt to 80 ml warm water, stirred clear, then into a dropper or spray bottle.$q$),
($q$Saline solution$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://drinksworld.com/saline-solution-for-cocktails/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for Drinksworld's own 80 g water to 20 g salt saline, the same strength as ours: up to 6 months (6 x 4 weeks) in a sealed dropper bottle in the fridge.$q$),
($q$Saline solution (10%)$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/articles/case-for-adding-salt-to-all-cocktail-recipes/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Little Red Door's low strength saline: distilled water to kosher salt 10:1 by weight, dashed into most drinks.$q$),
($q$Sangrita$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://feastandwest.com/sangrita/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$6 oz tomato, 4 oz orange and 2 oz lime juice (3:2:1) with 1 to 2 dashes hot sauce, a pinch each of salt and pepper and one halved jalapeño steeped 15 to 30 minutes. Scaled x 3.3 to 1.2 litres.$q$),
($q$Simple syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.diffordsguide.com/encyclopedia/3593/cocktails/2-to-1-rich-sugar-syrup-versus-1-to-1-simple-syrup$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$One part sugar to one part water (1:1); Difford's notes weighing gives a slightly sweeter syrup than measuring by volume. Scaled to 1 kg sugar.$q$),
($q$Simple syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://punchdrink.com/articles/not-too-sweet-ok-how-to-use-simple-demerara-cane-honey-agave-cocktail-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Simple is equal parts white sugar and water by weight, about 50 Brix. Agrees with Difford's.$q$),
($q$Simple syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://alcademics.com/simple-syrup-its-good-to-be-rich/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Side by side fridge test: plain 1:1 syrup lasted a month before clouding. We keep 3 weeks, inside that.$q$),
($q$Sour mix$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://vinepair.com/articles/sour-mix-cocktail-recipe/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$1 cup sugar boiled into 1 cup water, cooled, then mixed with 1/2 cup each lime and lemon juice. That syrup is about 1.5 cups, so 1.5 parts syrup to 1 part juice; scaled to 500 ml juice.$q$),
