($q$Spiced syrup$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://jawnsicooked.com/cocktails/fall-spiced-simple-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$1 cup water, 1 cup cane sugar, 1 tbsp honey, 1 cinnamon stick, 1 star anise, 2 cloves; simmer 5 minutes, cool, strain. Cups converted (240 ml, 200 g) and scaled to 500 ml water: 415 g sugar, 30 ml honey, 2 sticks, 2 star anise, 4 cloves.$q$),
($q$Spiced syrup$q$, $q$yield$q$, $q$https://jawnsicooked.com/cocktails/fall-spiced-simple-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$About 1.5 cups (360 ml) per cup of water; scaled to 500 ml water, about 750 ml.$q$),
($q$Spiced syrup$q$, $q$keeps$q$, $q$https://jawnsicooked.com/cocktails/fall-spiced-simple-syrup/$q$, $q$reference$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$Keep for this same recipe: airtight in the fridge, up to two months. We keep the shorter three weeks already set.$q$),
($q$Strawberry shrub$q$, $q$recipe$q$, $q$https://www.ccfruitandnuts.ucanr.edu/sites/default/files/2023-10/389540.pdf$q$, $q$law$q$, DATE '2026-10-13', $q$UC Master Food Preservers give equal parts fruit, sugar and vinegar (1:1:1) as the common shrub formula, and suggest white wine vinegar for delicately flavoured fruit. 500 g of each.$q$),
